TITLE:: DrumStep
SUMMARY:: One drum-grid column, with or without a hit.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/AmpCommand, Classes/BorderView, Classes/DrumProgrammer, Classes/GridSlider, Classes/PlayableNote, Classes/SwitchCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::DrumStep:: is one column of a LINK::Classes/DrumProgrammer:: row. It is not a view. It holds a LINK::Classes/GridSlider::, the column start time, the drum's MIDI note number, and a LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: when that square is a hit. An empty square still has a step, so LINK::Classes/SwitchCommand:: can turn it on. The slider shows the hit's amplitude: the top of the square is CODE::1:: and the bottom is CODE::0::. Left click or left drag sets that amplitude and turns the hit on. Dragging to CODE::0::, or a right click, turns it off. LINK::#-switch_:: takes an integer: CODE::1:: ensures a hit at velocity 100 and CODE::0:: clears one. An existing hit keeps its velocity. LINK::Classes/DrumProgrammer:: supplies the callbacks that add and remove the note from the sequence. A row with no MIDI note number ignores both mouse buttons.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a step and its square.

ARGUMENT:: noteNumber
MIDI note number for this drum, or CODE::nil:: for a row that has no sound yet.

ARGUMENT:: startTime
Column start time in beats.

ARGUMENT:: palette
The LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for the square colours.

ARGUMENT:: squareSize
Width and height of the square, in pixels.

ARGUMENT:: velocity
MIDI velocity used when CODE::1:: creates a new hit.

ARGUMENT:: hitDuration
Length of a new hit, in beats.

ARGUMENT:: addFunc
Called with the new LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: when a hit is created.

ARGUMENT:: removeFunc
Called with the LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: when a hit is cleared.

ARGUMENT:: existingNote
A LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: already stored for this column, or CODE::nil::. When present, the slider shows that note's amplitude and the add callback is not called.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::DrumStep:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: amp_
Sets the amplitude of this column. CODE::0:: clears the hit. Any other value in CODE::0:: to CODE::1:: ensures a hit and passes the clipped value to LINK::Classes/PlayableNote#-amp_::, which sets the MIDI velocity. The slider then shows that velocity mapped back to CODE::0::–CODE::1::.

ARGUMENT:: value
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::. Values outside CODE::0:: to CODE::1:: are clipped.

METHOD:: playableNote
The LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: for this column, or CODE::nil:: when the square is empty.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/PlayableNote::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: square
The square for this column.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/GridSlider::.

METHOD:: startTime
The column start time in beats.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::.

METHOD:: switch_
Sets whether this column is a hit. CODE::1:: creates a hit when the square is empty, with the velocity and duration given to LINK::#*new::, and calls the add callback. The slider then shows velocity 100, which is CODE::100/127:: of the square. If a hit is already there, it is left as it is. CODE::0:: removes a hit and calls the remove callback. The slider then shows amplitude CODE::0::. An empty square stays empty.

ARGUMENT:: value
An LINK::Classes/Integer::. CODE::1:: ensures a hit. CODE::0:: clears a hit.

PRIVATE:: init, prClearHit, prEnsureHit, prSetAmp, prSyncSlider
